Package: brouillet
Title: Reusable Contrast-Curve Colour Gradients
Version: 0.5.0
Authors@R:
    person("Your", "Name", email = "you@example.org", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Build a colour-gradient specification once and reuse it across
    plots. A contrast curve, parameterised by centre and width in relative
    units, controls where along the data range the colour change is
    concentrated, so a narrow band of interest can be expanded and the
    uninformative remainder compressed. Colours are interpolated in CIE Lab
    by default. Specifications convert to a value-to-colour function usable
    by any plotting system, or to 'ggplot2' fill and colour scales, and
    support two-sided out-of-range (clipping) colours shown as bands on the
    colourbar.
